can you verify the configuration for IPv6 mobility using mip6d?

the MN has two interfaces. eth0 connected to the 3f32::/64 network where
the HA and CN are, and another eth1 connected to a different network,
2f32::/64, routed with 3f32::/64

MN:

/etc/network/interfaces:

```
auto eth0
iface eth0 inet6 auto

auto eth1
iface eth1 inet6 auto
```

/usr/local/etc/mip6d.conf

```
NodeConfig MN;

DebugLevel 10;

OptimisticHandoff enabled;

DoRouteOptimizationMN enabled;

MnMaxHaBindingLife 60;

Interface "eth0" {
        MnIfPreference 1;
}
Interface "eth1" {
        MnIfPreference 2;
}

MnHomeLink "eth0" {
        HomeAgentAddress 3f32::2;
        HomeAddress 3f32::3/64;
}

UseMnHaIPsec disabled;

KeyMngMobCapability disabled;

IPsecPolicySet {
        HomeAgentAddress 3f32::2;
        HomeAddress 3f32::3/64;

        IPsecPolicy Mh UseESP 11 12;
        IPsecPolicy TunnelPayload UseESP 13 14;
        IPsecPolicy ICMP UseESP 15 16;
}
```

CN:

/etc/network/interfaces

```
allow-hotplug eth0
auto eth0
iface eth0 inet6 auto
```

/usr/local/etc/mip6d.conf

```
NodeConfig CN;

DebugLevel 10;

OptimisticHandoff disabled;

DoRouteOptimizationMN enabled;

MnMaxHaBindingLife 60;

Interface "eth0" {
    MnIfPreference 1;
}

UseMnHaIPsec disabled;
KeyMngMobCapability disabled;
```

HA:

/etc/network/interfaces

```
allow-hotplug eth0
auto eth0
iface eth0 inet6 static
    address 3f32::2/64
    gateway 3f32::1
```

/usr/local/etc/mip6d.conf

```
NodeConfig HA;

DebugLevel 10;

Interface "eth0";

BindingAclPolicy 3f32::3 allow;
DefaultBindingAclPolicy deny;

UseMnHaIPsec disabled;
KeyMngMobCapability disabled;
```

/etc/radvd.conf

```
interface eth0 {
        AdvSendAdvert on;
        MaxRtrAdvInterval 3;
        MinRtrAdvInterval 1;
        AdvIntervalOpt on;
        AdvHomeAgentFlag on;
        AdvHomeAgentInfo on;
        HomeAgentLifetime 1800;
        HomeAgentPreference 10;

        # Home agent address
        prefix 3f32::/64 {
                AdvRouterAddr on;
                AdvOnLink on;
                AdvAutonomous on;
        };
};
```


